0.195,0.263,0.253,0.253,0.259,0.193,0.23,0.223,0.361,0.209,0.155,-5.756,-7.605,null,-5.247,null,null,null,null,null,0.403,0.35,0.382,0.378,0.367,0.369,0.342,0.419,0.342,0.408,0.415,0.423,0.487,0.351,0.291,0.288,0.371,0.378,0.45,0.358,0.404,0.356,0.336,0.266,0.605,0.322,0.371,0.402,0.354,0.295,0.319,0.216,0.247,0.164,0.256,0.241,0.254,0.254,0.202,0.245,0.259,0.211,0.251,0.261,0.322,0.231,0.196,0.226,0.218,0.21,0.185,0.151,0.193,0.2,0.178,0.138,0.139,0.248,0.705,0.83],"nearFieldExcludedAtWaypoint":40,"fixedParameters":{"edgeSigmaPx":1.5,"edgeThreshold":4.0,"azStepDeg":2,"headingUncertaintyDeg":10.0,"elevationOffsetMaxDeg":0.5,"nearFieldM":150.0,"grid":"61 x 61 at 100 m, prior 1-2 km from the waypoint (seed 2021)","uncertaintyRule":"RMS <= best + 0.05 deg, min 50 m","ctxStepM":40.0,"ctxMaxKm":15.0,"molaStepM":250.0,"molaMaxKm":120.0,"minCellColumns":10,"minScoredAzimuths":20,"frameSpacingDeg":40.0,"frameRule":"NAVCAM_LEFT, same site+drive, full-width (5120 px) strip, |mastEl| <= 8 deg, LTST 9-16 h","hardwareMaskRoverAzDeg":null,"minScoredFractionOfValid":0.5,"successRule":"FIX = error <= 500 m and uncertainty <= 1000 m; WEAK = error < prior offset; else FAILED"},"assumptions":["Truth position AND attitude come from NASA's M20_waypoints.json entry matched by site+drive (not by sol); the waypoint yaw/pitch/roll rotation equals each frame's own attitude quaternion (max matrix element difference 1.4e-03). Waypoint = end-of-drive localization; its own accuracy is not stated by NASA in the file and is assumed to be metres to tens of metres.","Frames: all Navcam-left frames of this site+drive that pass the fixed usability rule; of those a deterministic greedy subset (boresight azimuths >= 40 deg apart, starting at the seed frame, clockwise) is downloaded to stay inside the download budget. 36 frames passed the rule, 4 used. Seed/'single frame' = the earliest-sclk usable frame.","Skyline traced per frame with the SAME settings as the single-frame tests (sigma 1.5 px, threshold 4.0, 5-px median smoothing, >12 px running-median outlier rejection); not tuned. Each frame's columns are converted to true azimuth/elevation with its own CAHVORE model and the waypoint attitude, binned to 2-deg cells (>= 10 traced columns, median elevation); frames are merged per cell by median. Cells with no frame or no accepted trace are NaN (null) and are not scored.","Rover-hardware rule: no azimuth sector is masked. On the development frames the rover deck/RTG appears only in the lowest part of the frame, well below the skyline, so the geometric rule is: nothing masked. Not examined for held-out frames before the run.","Matching: heading known to +-10 deg (11 shifts of 2 deg); one elevation offset per candidate (clipped to +-0.5 deg); azimuths whose predicted horizon forms closer than 150 m at the candidate are excluded for that candidate; score = RMS over scored azimuths. The same near-field and offset rules are used in all four ablation rows; only the frame set and the backdrop change. A candidate must score at least 20 azimuths AND 50% of the valid azimuths: this guard was added after the first development run, in which the single-frame best candidate scored only 20 of 48 azimuths because the near-field rule dropped the rest (a degenerate 'win'). It was not tuned on position error.","Horizon = max over CTX samples (40 m, to 15 km) and MOLA samples (250 m, to 120 km, only outside the CTX footprint or beyond 15 km), Mars curvature term, eye 2 m above the CTX elevation at the candidate. CTX minus MOLA at 400 random points inside the DTM: mean -3.6 m, std 24.9 m, so no vertical offset is applied. MOLA is 463 m/pixel and median-binned: it cannot represent terrain finer than that.","CTX part of horizons_ext is checked equal to skyline.horizons (imported, unchanged) at 24 candidates every run (max difference < 1e-6 deg).","A 20 m DTM cannot contain metre-scale rocks in the foreground; those rows of the skyline are part of the photo but not of the model.","Downloads this run: 4 images (cached ones not counted)."],"method":"Real Navcam frames (NASA/JPL-Caltech raw images), skyline traced and matched against CTX DTM + MOLA horizon; not simulated.","verdict":"FIX ACHIEVED (rule fixed before the held-out runs: FIX = error <= 500 m and uncertainty <= 1000 m; WEAK = error below the prior offset). Full method (panorama of 4 frames, 94% of azimuths scored, CTX + MOLA backdrop): error 51 m, uncertainty radius 50 m, min RMS 0.950 deg (prior offset 1757 m). Ablation errors (m): single/CTX 2853, single+MOLA 2085, panorama/CTX 51, full 51. At the waypoint itself the full-method RMS is 1.026 deg (residual median +0.23, 5-95% range -0.57 to +0.65 deg). One position, one run: not a statistical result."}